    'methodology.pillar_section_title': 'Understanding Each Category',
    'methodology.pillar_section_intro': 'Click on each category below to learn what it measures and how to interpret scores.',
    'methodology.pillar.sources_label': 'Data Sources:',
    'methodology.pillar.low_label': 'Low Score (1-3)',
    'methodology.pillar.high_label': 'High Score (8-10)',
    'methodology.pillar.conflict.title': 'Conflict (30%)',
    'methodology.pillar.conflict.description': 'Measures armed conflict intensity, militarization levels, government travel advisory warnings, and conflict-death counts from the Uppsala Conflict Data Program (UCDP), log-normalized so a single catastrophic year does not saturate the signal. This category carries the highest weight because active conflicts and government warnings pose the most immediate and severe risk to travelers. Includes advisory levels from 37 governments worldwide.',
    'methodology.pillar.conflict.sources': 'Global Peace Index scores, travel advisory levels from 37 government sources worldwide (US, UK, Canada, Australia, Germany, Netherlands, Japan, and 30 more), and UCDP Georeferenced Event Dataset battle-related and one-sided conflict-death counts via the Our World in Data mirror (CC-BY).',
    'methodology.pillar.conflict.low_score': 'Active or recent armed conflict, political instability, high militarization. Travelers face elevated physical security risks.',
    'methodology.pillar.conflict.high_score': 'Peaceful and politically stable, low conflict risk and minimal militarization. Generally safe from conflict-related threats.',
    'methodology.pillar.crime.title': 'Crime (25%)',
    'methodology.pillar.crime.description': 'Measures societal safety and security by blending the Global Peace Index\'s Safety & Security domain (67% of the pillar) with the World Bank\'s intentional-homicide rate (33%). The homicide signal\'s statistical precision is scaled by population, so a handful of homicides in a very small territory (our population-reliability model half-saturates around 200,000 people) is treated as statistical noise rather than a worse-than-war crime signal. This is distinct from the Governance pillar\'s rule-of-law measure: Crime reflects how safe day-to-day life and travel actually are, not how well courts and institutions function.',
    'methodology.pillar.crime.sources': 'Global Peace Index Safety & Security Score (Institute for Economics and Peace) — homicide rate, violent crime perception, and related indicators across 163 countries; World Bank intentional-homicide rate per 100,000 population, population-reliability scaled.',
    'methodology.pillar.crime.low_score': 'High homicide and violent-crime rates, high perceived criminality. Travelers face elevated risk of theft, assault, or worse, especially outside secured tourist areas.',
    'methodology.pillar.crime.high_score': 'Low homicide and violent-crime rates, low perceived criminality. Travelers generally experience routine, everyday safety with standard precautions.',
    'methodology.pillar.health.title': 'Health (20%)',
    'methodology.pillar.health.description': 'Measures healthcare system quality and epidemic or disease risk. Access to reliable healthcare and low disease prevalence are critical factors for traveler safety.',
    'methodology.pillar.health.sources': 'World Bank child mortality rate (proxy for healthcare quality), INFORM Health Risk Index, INFORM Epidemic Risk Index.',
    'methodology.pillar.health.low_score': 'Limited healthcare access, elevated disease or epidemic risk. Travelers may face challenges obtaining medical care.',
    'methodology.pillar.health.high_score': 'Strong healthcare infrastructure, low epidemic risk. Quality medical care is accessible and disease risks are minimal.',
    'methodology.pillar.governance.title': 'Governance (15%)',
    'methodology.pillar.governance.description': 'Measures the rule of law, institutional effectiveness, and corruption levels. Well-governed countries with reliable courts and low corruption provide more predictable and safer environments for travelers, including access to legal recourse if something goes wrong.',
    'methodology.pillar.governance.sources': 'V-Dem Rule of Law Index, V-Dem Public Administration Quality, V-Dem Political Corruption Index (inverted), INFORM Governance Index.',
    'methodology.pillar.governance.low_score': 'Weak rule of law, high corruption, governance fragility. Travelers may find police and courts offer limited protection or recourse, alongside unreliable public services.',
    'methodology.pillar.governance.high_score': 'Strong rule of law, effective and transparent institutions, corruption well controlled. Travelers benefit from reliable legal recourse and public services.',
    'methodology.pillar.environment.title': 'Environment (10%)',
    'methodology.pillar.environment.description': 'Measures natural hazard exposure and environmental health risks. While often seasonal or localized, natural disasters and poor air quality can significantly impact travel safety. Includes ReliefWeb humanitarian disasters and GDACS natural disaster alerts for near-realtime monitoring.',
    'methodology.pillar.environment.sources': 'World Bank Air Pollution (PM2.5), INFORM Natural Hazard Risk Index, INFORM Climate Risk Index, ReliefWeb Active Humanitarian Disasters, GDACS Natural Disaster Alerts.',
    'methodology.pillar.environment.low_score': 'High exposure to natural disasters, severe air pollution, climate-related hazards. Travelers should monitor weather and environmental conditions closely.',
    'methodology.pillar.environment.high_score': 'Low natural hazard risk, good air quality. Environmental conditions are generally favorable for travelers.',
